## Compound Conditions

Real decisions are rarely about one thing. Boolean operators let you combine multiple checks:

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let age = 25;
  let has_license = true;

  if age >= 18 && has_license {
    io.println("You can drive!");
  }

  return 0;
}
```

### Building Complex Conditions

```xiom
// AND: all conditions must be true
if score >= 60 && score <= 100 {
  io.println("Valid score");
}

// OR: any condition can be true
if day == "Saturday" || day == "Sunday" {
  io.println("It's the weekend!");
}

// NOT: reverse a condition
if !is_banned {
  io.println("Welcome back!");
}

// Combined: (A AND B) OR C
if (is_admin && is_active) || is_owner {
  io.println("Access granted");
}
```

### Parentheses Matter

```xiom
// Different meanings!
if (a && b) || c { ... }  // (both a AND b) OR c
if a && (b || c) { ... }  // a AND (either b OR c)
```

When in doubt, use parentheses to make your intent explicit.

### Creating Self-Documenting Conditions

```xiom
let is_valid_age = age >= 0 && age <= 150;
let is_valid_email = email == "valid@example.com";
let can_register = is_valid_age && is_valid_email;

if can_register {
  io.println("Registration complete!");
}
```

### Truth Tables Review

| A | B | A && B | A \|\| B | !A |
|---|---|--------|---------|-----|
| T | T | T | T | F |
| T | F | F | T | F |
| F | T | F | T | T |
| F | F | F | F | T |

### Short-Circuit Still Applies

```xiom
// If is_admin is true, check_permission() is never called (OR short-circuits)
if is_admin || check_permission() {
  io.println("Access granted");
}
```

